  "observed": {
    "summary": "File > Export Audio > Export Wav Files To... (a save dialog taking a base file name) exported one WAV per track in one operation: <base>_<TrackName>.wav, i.e. Tenor, Lead, Baritone, Bass (four files). Each is mono, 16-bit, 44100 Hz and exactly as long as its own part: Tenor 211681 frames (4.8 s, 8 notes), Lead 185221 (4.2 s, 7), Baritone 158761 (3.6 s, 6), Bass 132301 (3.0 s, 5), so the stems are not padded to the song length. The four stems differ in content, and a repeated export of the Tenor track was byte-identical. Muting a track left it out of the export (3 files); soloing a track exported only that track (1 file). A track with no singer was exported as an empty zero-frame 46-byte WAV with no error. Rendering with the default phonemizer succeeded. Other menu items (Export Wav Files, Mixdown To Wav File) were not exercised.",
